  "title": "Directional source and receiver capability pilot",
  "benchmarkMeta": {
    "status": "exploratory",
    "locked": true,
    "notes": [
      "Predeclared one-repeat pilot with six role-specific model assignments and twelve balanced speaking orders per assignment.",
      "Every run uses the same ego-depletion question, three instructed agents, three neutral agents, standard shared memory, 18 calls, and temperature 0.",
      "Role prompts, numeric profiles, agent identities, question, condition, call budget, and speaking orders remain fixed. Only the model assigned to each role changes.",
      "Primary outcomes are final neutral-agent endorsement, any neutral adoption, complete neutral adoption, and instructed-role retention.",
      "Primary contrasts swap the instructed-agent model while fixing the neutral-agent model, and swap the neutral-agent model while fixing the instructed-agent model.",
      "The open-weight bridge uses Llama 3.3 70B Instruct through OpenRouter.",
      "No scaling claim will be made from this pilot alone. Expansion requires a separately declared repeat cohort after inspecting floor and ceiling behavior."
    ]
  },
